# Release-gate declarations (user decision 2026-10-28; research/PROPOSAL-RELEASE-GATE.md). DECLARED by subject, never inferred from mentions.
# `tools/gate.sh --release` runs: the Node gate + the SMOKE tests below + the browser tests of every group whose globs match a file changed since origin/main
# (+ a browser test whose own tests/NAME.cjs changed). CI then runs everything and deploys only if green.
# Syntax (one per line, fields separated by ' | '):
#   smoke | test test ...                  always run locally
#   group NAME | glob glob ... | test ...  a changed file matching ANY glob adds these tests (union over all matching groups). NONE = nothing to run, ALL = the whole browser tier.
#   ci-only | test test ...                browser tests deliberately run only in CI (a browser test in no group and not here fails the lint)
# Globs are fnmatch patterns on repo-relative paths (`*` also matches `/`). `gate.sh --lint` fails if a tracked file matches no group, or a test named here is not in tests/BROWSER.
smoke | season2-smoke@PART=A,C,E,F,G season2-smoke@PART=D season2-smoke@PART=Bweurope,Bnamerica,Bsasia,Baotearoa season2-smoke@PART=Bafrica,Bsamerica,Beasia,Boceania,Bpatagonia hubscreen saveloss records-screen missionscreen hudlayout tourgiveup textfit crash
